We need produce ST code for FB_HmiAccess. Need precise per requirements.

Let's derive.

Inputs: SessionValid BOOL, Role USINT, Page USINT, WriteReq BOOL, WriteValue LREAL.
Outputs: ViewAllowed, WriteAllowed, Accepted, Denied BOOL; ParamValue LREAL.

Need initial ParamValue = 0.0. In ST FB, internal var initialization? We can declare ParamValue : LREAL := 0.0; as output with init. STruC++ supports initialization. Better declare output ParamValue : LREAL := 0.0.

Logic each scan:
valid := SessionValid AND (Role = 1 OR Role=2 OR Role=3).

View permissions:
Role 1: pages 1,2
Role 2: pages 1,2,4
Role 3: pages 1,2,3,4
others none.

ViewAllowed := valid AND ... page.

Write : SessionValid AND Role in {2,3} AND Page = 4. Note V? write formula uses SessionValid AND Role∈{2,3} AND Page=4. Since role 2/3 valid anyway. So WriteAllowed := SessionValid AND (Role=2 OR Role=3) AND Page=4. Could use valid but same.

Accept := WriteReq AND WriteAllowed AND (WriteValue >= 0.0) AND (WriteValue <= 100.0). All finite assumed.

Accepted := accept? Requirement 3: On acceptance update ParamValue and set Accepted TRUE Denied FALSE.
Requirement 4: With no WriteReq, Accepted=Denied=FALSE. Reject any requested write with insufficient permission or out-of-range value: Denied TRUE Accepted FALSE preserve. P04: Denied <-> (WriteReq & !accept). So exactly:
Accepted := accept;
Denied := WriteReq AND NOT accept;

If accept then ParamValue := WriteValue.

Check P06: G(!accept -> parameterHeld). If not accept, ParamValue held. Our code only updates when accept. Good.

Ordering in ST: Need compute booleans. ParamValue update if accept. Accepted/Denied each scan.

Potential issue ParamValue output used in pre value hold. Fine.

Need preserve interface names/directions/types exactly. Use FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_HmiAccess with VAR_INPUT ... VAR_OUTPUT ParamValue LREAL := 0.0. Is init on output allowed? Yes.

Need "only actual ST, no test driver". Output JSON summary and code.

Let's write with auxiliary local booleans maybe.

FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_HmiAccess
VAR_INPUT
  SessionValid : BOOL;
  Role : USINT;
  Page : USINT;
  WriteReq : BOOL;
  WriteValue : LREAL;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
  ViewAllowed : BOOL;
  WriteAllowed : BOOL;
  Accepted : BOOL;
  Denied : BOOL;
  ParamValue : LREAL := 0.0;
END_VAR
VAR
  validSession : BOOL;
  acceptWrite : BOOL;
END_VAR

validSession := SessionValid AND ((Role = 1) OR (Role = 2) OR (Role = 3));

ViewAllowed := FALSE;
IF validSession THEN
  CASE Role OF
    1:
      IF (Page = 1) OR (Page = 2) THEN ViewAllowed := TRUE; END_IF;
    2:
      IF (Page = 1) OR (Page = 2) OR (Page = 4) THEN ViewAllowed := TRUE; END_IF;
    3:
      IF (Page = 1) OR (Page = 2) OR (Page = 3) OR (Page = 4) THEN ViewAllowed := TRUE; END_IF;
  ELSE
    ViewAllowed := FALSE;
  END_CASE;
END_IF;

Alternatively IF/ELSIF. CASE ELSE no colon (requirement). This is okay. But "CASE的ELSE后不要加冒号" means not `ELSE:`. We'll write `ELSE`.

WriteAllowed := SessionValid AND ((Role = 2) OR (Role = 3)) AND (Page = 4);

acceptWrite := WriteReq AND WriteAllowed AND (WriteValue >= 0.0) AND (WriteValue <= 100.0);

Accepted := acceptWrite;
Denied := WriteReq AND NOT acceptWrite;

IF acceptWrite THEN
  ParamValue := WriteValue;
END_IF;

Need ensure BOOL operators use AND OR NOT. In ST, `NOT` precedence? fine.

Potential P04: Denied <-> (WriteReq & !accept). Here accept is acceptWrite. Yes.

Potential concern if WriteReq true and accept false, Denied true. Good.

ViewAllowed formula: V AND Page∈AllowedPages(Role). For other roles empty. We set false.

One nuance: requirements "Role 1 is user, 2 operator and 3 administrator; every other role is unauthorized." Good.

No need TON/R_TRIG.

Need maybe mention no authenticated passwords.

JSON only. summary in Chinese maybe. code complete ST. Ensure code string escaped newlines.

We should produce valid JSON. Use double quotes; code contains double quotes? No. Newlines as \n.

Let's craft summary concise.

Need ensure code uses `:=` etc.

Could simplify ViewAllowed with IF. Since only 4 pages.

Let's ensure initial ParamValue = 0.0. Output initialization in declaration. In STruC++ maybe output init supported. Could also use internal firstScan? But requirement initial. Declaration `ParamValue : LREAL := 0.0;` is typical. If not supported? STruC++ supports variable initialization.

Potential issue output variable cannot have initial value? In IEC 61131-3, VAR_OUTPUT can have initial value? In some compilers, outputs can have init. STruC++ likely supports. If not, declare internal var and assign, but must have ParamValue output exact. We can use `VAR_OUTPUT ParamValue : LREAL := 0.0;`. Fine.

Need no extra types.

